{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChLdbwXwteeThb2Rjxy7G","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01E6qYg5mfyEix2MBqwZ9roU","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/srv/hwebench/clones/claude-fable-5_2_xhigh-v2-rep1/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261123-002-r1s1/cores/bench/rtl/muldiv.sv","old_string":"// RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS: same FSM and handshake, but every M-op takes the\n// short S_MUL path (fixed 2-cycle latency) and the result is riscv-formal's\n// ALTOPS stand-in computed from the captured operands. Real arithmetic is\n// covered by test_muldiv.py, cosim and `make formal-deep`.\n//\n// Latency:        MUL* 2 extra cycles; DIV*/REM* 35 extra cycles.","new_string":"// RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS: same FSM and handshake, but every M-op takes the\n// multiplier's path (capture -> S_DONE, fixed 1 extra cycle) and the result\n// is riscv-formal's ALTOPS stand-in computed from the captured operands.\n// A 35-cycle divide could not retire inside the 20-step BMC window. Real\n// arithmetic and real divide latency are covered by test_muldiv.py, cosim\n// and `make formal-deep`.\n//\n// Latency:        MUL* 1 extra cycle; DIV*/REM* 35 extra cycles."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":784,"cache_read_input_tokens":151768,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":784},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"23fe396e-9186-4976-a3eb-d44c06478b93","uuid":"68242aaa-9ba0-4647-b6c2-f0bfcbfb1849","timestamp":"2026-11-23T22:15:58.922Z","request_id":"req_011ChLdbwQWLWoWz4Tiwvgmg"}
{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01E6qYg5mfyEix2MBqwZ9roU", "type": "tool_result", "content": "The file /srv/hwebench/clones/claude-fable-5_2_xhigh-v2-rep1/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261123-002-r1s1/cores/bench/rtl/muldiv.sv has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "23fe396e-9186-4976-a3eb-d44c06478b93", "uuid": "74b18258-490d-43a0-ad6a-829467b62356", "timestamp": "2026-11-23T22:15:58.937Z", "tool_use_result": {"filePath": "/srv/hwebench/clones/claude-fable-5_2_xhigh-v2-rep1/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261123-002-r1s1/cores/bench/rtl/muldiv.sv", "oldString": "// RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS: same FSM and handshake, but every M-op takes the\n// short S_MUL path (fixed 2-cycle latency) and the result is riscv-formal's\n// ALTOPS stand-in computed from the captured operands. Real arithmetic is\n// covered by test_muldiv.py, cosim and `make formal-deep`.\n//\n// Latency:        MUL* 2 extra cycles; DIV*/REM* 35 extra cycles.", "newString": "// RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS: same FSM and handshake, but every M-op takes the\n// multiplier's path (capture -> S_DONE, fixed 1 extra cycle) and the result\n// is riscv-formal's ALTOPS stand-in computed from the captured operands.\n// A 35-cycle divide could not retire inside the 20-step BMC window. Real\n// arithmetic and real divide latency are covered by test_muldiv.py, cosim\n// and `make formal-deep`.\n//\n// Latency:        MUL* 1 extra cycle; DIV*/REM* 35 extra cycles.", "originalFile": "// rtl/muldiv.sv\n//\n// Sequential RV32M unit. Multiply / divide / remainder run here over\n// several cycles while the M instruction waits in ID/EX (ex_stage raises\n// ex_busy until `done`), so no `*`, `/` or `%` sits in the single-cycle\n// forward -> ALU -> EX/MEM loop.\n//\n// Handshake:\n//   start : level, \"an M-op is in EX\". Honoured only in S_IDLE; that cycle's\n//           op/a/b (post-forward operands) are captured at the clock edge.\n//   done  : high while the result is valid and waiting to be consumed.\n//   ack   : EX/MEM captures the result this cycle -> back to S_IDLE.\n//\n// Multiplier: ONE 33x33 signed multiply. Operand sign bits are\n// a[31]&a_signed / b[31]&b_signed. Operands are registered (DSP input\n// registers); the product is read by EX/MEM in the next cycle, so a MUL*\n// costs 1 extra cycle in EX. (`make timing`: operand reg -> DSP -> EX/MEM\n// is not among the worst paths, so the product register was dropped.)\n//\n// Divider: radix-2 restoring on magnitudes, 1 bit/cycle:\n//   capture (raw a/b + sign flags) -> S_DPRE (|a|, |b|) -> 32 x S_DRUN\n//   -> S_DPOST (sign fix) -> S_DONE.\n// RV32M corner cases fall out of the algorithm with one rule: negate the\n// quotient only if the signs differ AND b != 0.\n//   x / 0        -> all ones      x % 0        -> x\n//   INT_MIN / -1 -> INT_MIN       INT_MIN % -1 -> 0\n//\n// RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS: same FSM and handshake, but every M-op takes the\n// short S_MUL path (fixed 2-cycle latency) and the result is riscv-formal's\n// ALTOPS stand-in computed from the captured operands. Real arithmetic is\n// covered by test_muldiv.py, cosim and `make formal-deep`.\n//\n// Latency:        MUL* 2 extra cycles; DIV*/REM* 35 extra cycles.\n// RVFI fields:    feeds rd_wdata of every M-extension instruction.\nmodule muldiv (\n  input  logic        clock,\n  input  logic        reset,\n  input  logic        start,\n  input  logic        ack,\n  input  logic [4:0]  op,\n  input  logic [31:0] a,\n  input  logic [31:0] b,\n  output logic        done,\n  output logic [31:0] result\n);\n\n  localparam logic [2:0] S_IDLE  = 3'd0;\n  localparam logic [2:0] S_DONE  = 3'd2;\n`ifndef RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\n  localparam logic [2:0] S_DPRE  = 3'd3;\n  localparam logic [2:0] S_DRUN  = 3'd4;\n  localparam logic [2:0] S_DPOST = 3'd5;\n`endif\n\n  logic [2:0] state_q;\n  logic       capture;\n\n  assign capture = (state_q == S_IDLE) && start;\n  assign done    = (state_q == S_DONE);\n\n`ifdef RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\n  // ── ALTOPS: fixed 2-cycle latency for every M-op ──────────────────────\n  logic [4:0]  op_q;\n  logic [31:0] a_q;\n  logic [31:0] b_q;\n  logic [31:0] alt_d;\n\n  always_comb begin\n    case (op_q)\n      ALU_MUL:    alt_d = (a_q + b_q) ^ 32'h5876063e;\n      ALU_MULH:   alt_d = (a_q + b_q) ^ 32'hf6583fb7;\n      ALU_MULHU:  alt_d = (a_q + b_q) ^ 32'h949ce5e8;\n      ALU_MULHSU: alt_d = (a_q - b_q) ^ 32'hecfbe137;\n      ALU_DIV:    alt_d = (a_q - b_q) ^ 32'h7f8529ec;\n      ALU_DIVU:   alt_d = (a_q - b_q) ^ 32'h10e8fd70;\n      ALU_REM:    alt_d = (a_q - b_q) ^ 32'h8da68fa5;\n      ALU_REMU:   alt_d = (a_q - b_q) ^ 32'h3138d0e1;\n      default:    alt_d = 32'b0;\n    endcase\n  end\n\n  always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\n    if (reset) begin\n      state_q <= S_IDLE;\n    end else begin\n      case (state_q)\n        S_IDLE:  if (start) state_q <= S_DONE;\n        S_DONE:  if (ack)   state_q <= S_IDLE;\n        default: state_q <= S_IDLE;\n      endcase\n    end\n  end\n\n  always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\n    if (capture) begin\n      op_q <= op;\n      a_q  <= a;\n      b_q  <= b;\n    end\n  end\n\n  assign result = alt_d;\n\n`else\n  // ── Real arithmetic ───────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  logic op_is_div;      // DIV / DIVU / REM / REMU\n  logic op_is_rem;      // REM / REMU\n  logic op_div_signed;  // DIV / REM\n  logic op_a_signed;    // MULH / MULHSU\n  logic op_b_signed;    // MULH\n\n  always_comb begin\n    op_is_div     = (op == ALU_DIV) || (op == ALU_DIVU)\n                 || (op == ALU_REM) || (op == ALU_REMU);\n    op_is_rem     = (op == ALU_REM) || (op == ALU_REMU);\n    op_div_signed = (op == ALU_DIV) || (op == ALU_REM);\n    op_a_signed   = (op == ALU_MULH) || (op == ALU_MULHSU);\n    op_b_signed   = (op == ALU_MULH);\n  end\n\n  // Multiplier: registered operands -> 33x33 signed -> result mux. The\n  // product is read by EX/MEM in the cycle after capture (S_DONE).\n  logic signed [32:0] mul_a_q;\n  logic signed [32:0] mul_b_q;\n  // 33x33 signed product is 66 bits; bits [65:64] are sign copies.\n  /* verilator lint_off UNUSEDSIGNAL */\n  logic signed [65:0] mul_p_q;\n  /* verilator lint_on UNUSEDSIGNAL */\n  logic               mul_low_q;   // MUL (low half) vs MULH* (high half)\n\n  always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\n    if (capture) begin\n      mul_a_q   <= $signed({a[31] & op_a_signed, a});\n      mul_b_q   <= $signed({b[31] & op_b_signed, b});\n      mul_low_q <= (op == ALU_MUL);\n    end\n  end\n\n  assign mul_p_q = mul_a_q * mul_b_q;\n\n  // Divider state.\n  logic [31:0] quo_q;      // dividend, shifts out MSB-first; quotient shifts in\n  logic [31:0] rem_q;      // partial remainder (always < divisor when b != 0)\n  logic [31:0] dvs_q;      // divisor magnitude\n  logic [4:0]  cnt_q;\n  logic        a_neg_q;    // signed op and a < 0\n  logic        b_neg_q;    // signed op and b < 0\n  logic        b_zero_q;\n  logic        is_div_q;\n  logic        is_rem_q;\n\n  // Trial subtract: {rem, next dividend bit} - divisor. The true difference\n  // lies in (-2^32, 2^32), so bit 32 of the 33-bit result is its sign.\n  logic [32:0] sub;\n  assign sub = {rem_q, quo_q[31]} - {1'b0, dvs_q};\n\n  // Sign fix (shared negator).\n  logic [31:0] fix_val;\n  logic        fix_neg;\n  logic [31:0] fix_out;\n  always_comb begin\n    fix_val = is_rem_q ? rem_q : quo_q;\n    fix_neg = is_rem_q ? a_neg_q : ((a_neg_q ^ b_neg_q) && !b_zero_q);\n    fix_out = fix_neg ? (32'b0 - fix_val) : fix_val;\n  end\n\n  always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\n    if (reset) begin\n      state_q <= S_IDLE;\n    end else begin\n      case (state_q)\n        S_IDLE:  if (start) state_q <= op_is_div ? S_DPRE : S_DONE;\n        S_DPRE:  state_q <= S_DRUN;\n        S_DRUN:  if (cnt_q == 5'd31) state_q <= S_DPOST;\n        S_DPOST: state_q <= S_DONE;\n        S_DONE:  if (ack) state_q <= S_IDLE;\n        default: state_q <= S_IDLE;\n      endcase\n    end\n  end\n\n  always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\n    if (capture) begin\n      quo_q    <= a;\n      dvs_q    <= b;\n      a_neg_q  <= op_div_signed && a[31];\n      b_neg_q  <= op_div_signed && b[31];\n      is_div_q <= op_is_div;\n      is_rem_q <= op_is_rem;\n    end else if (state_q == S_DPRE) begin\n      // Magnitudes. INT_MIN negates to 0x8000_0000, which is the right\n      // unsigned magnitude.\n      quo_q    <= a_neg_q ? (32'b0 - quo_q) : quo_q;\n      dvs_q    <= b_neg_q ? (32'b0 - dvs_q) : dvs_q;\n      b_zero_q <= (dvs_q == 32'b0);\n      rem_q    <= 32'b0;\n      cnt_q    <= 5'd0;\n    end else if (state_q == S_DRUN) begin\n      if (!sub[32]) begin\n        rem_q <= sub[31:0];\n        quo_q <= {quo_q[30:0], 1'b1};\n      end else begin\n        rem_q <= {rem_q[30:0], quo_q[31]};\n        quo_q <= {quo_q[30:0], 1'b0};\n      end\n      cnt_q <= cnt_q + 5'd1;\n    end else if (state_q == S_DPOST) begin\n      quo_q <= fix_out;   // final DIV*/REM* result lives in quo_q\n    end\n  end\n\n  assign result = is_div_q  ? quo_q\n                : mul_low_q ? mul_p_q[31:0]\n                            : mul_p_q[63:32];\n`endif\n\nendmodule\n", "structuredPatch": [{"oldStart": 26, "oldLines": 11, "newStart": 26, "newLines": 13, "lines": [" //   INT_MIN / -1 -> INT_MIN       INT_MIN % -1 -> 0", " //", " // RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS: same FSM and handshake, but every M-op takes the", "-// short S_MUL path (fixed 2-cycle latency) and the result is riscv-formal's", "-// ALTOPS stand-in computed from the captured operands. Real arithmetic is", "-// covered by test_muldiv.py, cosim and `make formal-deep`.", "+// multiplier's path (capture -> S_DONE, fixed 1 extra cycle) and the result", "+// is riscv-formal's ALTOPS stand-in computed from the captured operands.", "+// A 35-cycle divide could not retire inside the 20-step BMC window. Real", "+// arithmetic and real divide latency are covered by test_muldiv.py, cosim", "+// and `make formal-deep`."