{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-fable-5-2", "id": "msg_011ChLdfJutvVPJHo3Kh6sDM", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01J19txV4uKaf59EEhhTRhqJ", "name": "Write", "input": {"file_path": "/srv/hwebench/clones/claude-fable-5_2_xhigh-v2-rep1/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261123-002-r1s1/cores/bench/implementation_notes.md", "content": "# Implementation notes — multi-cycle M-unit behind an EX-stall handshake\n\n## What changed\n\n- **rtl/muldiv.sv (new)** — sequential RV32M unit, ports\n  `clock, reset, start, ack, op[4:0] (alu_op), a, b -> done, result`.\n  - `start` is a level (\"M-op in EX\"), honoured only in `S_IDLE`; that\n    cycle's post-forward operands are captured. `done` = `S_DONE`; `ack`\n    (= `!stall_ex_mem`) returns the FSM to idle on the cycle EX/MEM captures.\n  - Divider: radix-2 restoring on magnitudes, 1 bit/cycle. capture (raw\n    a/b + sign flags) -> `S_DPRE` (|a|, |b|, b==0 flag) -> 32 x `S_DRUN`\n    (33-bit trial subtract + shift) -> `S_DPOST` (shared negator, result\n    written back into `quo_q`) -> `S_DONE`. 35 extra cycles. The single\n    corner-case rule is \"negate quotient only if signs differ AND b != 0\".\n  - Multiplier: ONE 33x33 signed multiply (sign bits `a[31]&a_signed`,\n    `b[31]&b_signed`), operands registered, 2 DSPs (was 6).\n  - `ifdef RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS`: same FSM/handshake, every M-op takes the\n    multiplier path (capture -> DONE) and the result is the ALTOPS formula\n    of the captured operands.\n- **rtl/alu.sv** — M arms deleted (real and ALTOPS); RV32I only.\n- **rtl/core_pkg.sv / decoder.sv / id_stage.sv** — new `ctrl_t.is_muldiv`,\n  set only inside the already-validated `funct7==0000001` R-type arm.\n  Decoder legality unchanged.\n- **rtl/id_stage.sv** — when ID/EX holds (`stall && !flush`) it writes the\n  post-forward `rs1/rs2` from EX back into `ID/EX.rs?_val` (operand\n  staleness fix; keeps `rvfi_rs?_rdata` right after the producers drain).\n- **rtl/ex_stage.sv** — instantiates `muldiv`, `ex_busy = m_op && !done`,\n  muldiv result muxed into `EX/MEM.alu_result`, new `bubble` input\n  (EX/MEM <= '0; dmem-stall hold keeps priority), exports forwarded rs1/rs2.\n- **rtl/hazard_unit.sv** — `ex_busy` ORed into `stall_if`/`stall_id`; new\n  `bubble_ex_mem = ex_busy && !dmem_stall`; `flush_if = imem_stall` only.\n- **rtl/if_stage.sv** — `redirect` removed from the IF/ID NOP mux *and*\n  from `out.valid` (item 6). Redirect acts only via the PC mux and\n  `flush_id`.\n- **rtl/core.sv** — wiring only. Top-level IO unchanged (nret=1).\n- **test/test_muldiv.py (new)** — every M-ext vector from test_alu.py\n  ported verbatim through the clocked handshake, plus back-to-back mixed\n  ops, result-held-until-ack, and a 46-vector corner/random sweep per op\n  against a Python RV32M reference (operand inputs are scrambled after the\n  capture cycle; exact latency asserted).\n- **test/test_alu.py** — RV32I vectors kept; M vectors moved; one test\n  pins that M encodings now fall to the ALU default.\n- **test/test_pipeline.py** — `muldiv.sv` added to sources; 5 new cases\n  (operands forwarded from EX/MEM + MEM/WB incl. RVFI rs*_rdata, result\n  consumed immediately, M-op behind a load, back-to-back MUL/DIV/REM incl.\n  div/rem by zero, wrong-path M-op after a taken branch).\n\n## Deviations from the hypothesis plan\n\n1. **MUL is 1 extra cycle, not 2.** I first built the contract's 2-extra-\n   cycle version (registered operands + registered product) and measured\n   it: `make timing` = 60.25 MHz, worst path MEM/WB.rd -> forward_unit ->\n   ALU -> dmem address, multiplier not in the top 5. The contract allows\n   cutting to 1 extra cycle in exactly that case, so I dropped the product\n   register: 62.39 MHz, 538 FFs (was 603), worst path now regfile -> EX\n   branch compare -> redirect -> ID/EX. Both numbers are placement\n   option 0 only (single run each); the evaluator takes the median of 3\n   options, so the ~2 MHz difference is within P&R noise — the claim is\n   only \"not slower\", plus one fewer cycle per MUL.\n2. **ALTOPS latency is 1 extra cycle, not the fixed 2** — it follows the\n   multiplier path so the formal model and the real MUL share one FSM path.\n3. **No `busy` output on muldiv** (unused by ex_stage; an unconnected pin\n   is a `-Wall` lint warning). No separate `result_q` register: the divide\n   result lives in `quo_q`, the multiply result is muxed from the product.\n4. **`out.valid` is no longer gated by `redirect`** (the hypothesis said it\n   \"may still be\"). It is redundant: on redirect ID/EX is either zeroed by\n   `flush_id` or held by dmem stall, never loaded.\n5. `op` is the 5-bit `alu_op` (decoded into flags at capture), not funct3.\n\n## Verification status (all on the final 1-extra-cycle RTL unless noted)\n\n- `verilator --lint-only -Wall`: clean.\n- cocotb (`pytest cores/bench/test`): 6/6 runners pass; test_muldiv 25/25,\n  test_pipeline 16/16.\n- `make cosim` (run as `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`): passed, 2 ELFs\n  (selftest with/without stalls + CoreMark CRCs). Plain `make cosim`\n  fails to *build* here because the Makefile's `cosim-build` prerequisite\n  defaults to NRET=2 while this core is nret=1 — pre-existing, unrelated\n  to this change; `tools.eval.cosim` sets NRET itself.\n- `bash formal/run_all.sh` (nret=1 auto-detect, ALTOPS):\n  - 2-extra-cycle version: **53 passed, 0 failed**.\n  - final 1-extra-cycle version: see \"Formal re-run\" below.\n- `make timing TARGET=bench` (Gowin, place option 0): baseline 5.44 MHz /\n  12312 LUT4 -> **62.39 MHz, 2381 logic, 538 FF, 2 DSP**.\n\n## Concerns\n\n- Fmax landed at ~60 MHz at option 0, above the hypothesis's 45-50 MHz\n  estimate, but it is one placement seed; not the scored median.\n- CoreMark iterations/cycle was not measured locally (cosim only checks\n  CRCs/RVFI), so the predicted ~1-3% cycle cost is unverified here.\n- `make formal-deep` (non-ALTOPS, proves the real multiplier/divider) was\n  not run — too slow for the 30-minute budget, and a 35-cycle divide\n  cannot retire inside a 20-step BMC anyway. Real arithmetic is covered by\n  test_muldiv.py and cosim only.\n- The DSP now has input registers but no output register; if a later\n  change shortens the two current worst paths, operand reg -> DSP ->\n  EX/MEM may become the limiter and the product register (S_MUL state)\n  would need to come back.\n"}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1040, "cache_read_input_tokens": 159114, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1040}, "output_tokens": 5, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "23fe396e-9186-4976-a3eb-d44c06478b93", "uuid": "3c186e81-db18-4d35-85db-baf852c4fc74", "timestamp": "2026-11-23T22:16:50.431Z", "request_id": "req_011ChLdfJkUYLKSw3B4ecrwF"}
{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01J19txV4uKaf59EEhhTRhqJ", "type": "tool_result", "content": "File created successfully at: /srv/hwebench/clones/claude-fable-5_2_xhigh-v2-rep1/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261123-002-r1s1/cores/bench/implementation_notes.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "23fe396e-9186-4976-a3eb-d44c06478b93", "uuid": "7d79347d-ba4a-43af-8641-9c24833ce730", "timestamp": "2026-11-23T22:16:50.442Z", "tool_use_result": {"type": "create", "filePath": "/srv/hwebench/clones/claude-fable-5_2_xhigh-v2-rep1/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261123-002-r1s1/cores/bench/implementation_notes.md", "content": "# Implementation notes — multi-cycle M-unit behind an EX-stall handshake\n\n## What changed\n\n- **rtl/muldiv.sv (new)** — sequential RV32M unit, ports\n  `clock, reset, start, ack, op[4:0] (alu_op), a, b -> done, result`.\n  - `start` is a level (\"M-op in EX\"), honoured only in `S_IDLE`; that\n    cycle's post-forward operands are captured. `done` = `S_DONE`; `ack`\n    (= `!stall_ex_mem`) returns the FSM to idle on the cycle EX/MEM captures.\n  - Divider: radix-2 restoring on magnitudes, 1 bit/cycle. capture (raw\n    a/b + sign flags) -> `S_DPRE` (|a|, |b|, b==0 flag) -> 32 x `S_DRUN`\n    (33-bit trial subtract + shift) -> `S_DPOST` (shared negator, result\n    written back into `quo_q`) -> `S_DONE`. 35 extra cycles. The single\n    corner-case rule is \"negate quotient only if signs differ AND b != 0\".\n  - Multiplier: ONE 33x33 signed multiply (sign bits `a[31]&a_signed`,\n    `b[31]&b_signed`), operands registered, 2 DSPs (was 6).\n  - `ifdef RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS`: same FSM/handshake, every M-op takes the\n    multiplier path (capture -> DONE) and the result is the ALTOPS formula\n    of the captured operands.\n- **rtl/alu.sv** — M arms deleted (real and ALTOPS); RV32I only.\n- **rtl/core_pkg.sv / decoder.sv / id_stage.sv** — new `ctrl_t.is_muldiv`,\n  set only inside the already-validated `funct7==0000001` R-type arm.\n  Decoder legality unchanged.\n- **rtl/id_stage.sv** — when ID/EX holds (`stall && !flush`) it writes the\n  post-forward `rs1/rs2` from EX back into `ID/EX.rs?_val` (operand\n  staleness fix; keeps `rvfi_rs?_rdata` right after the producers drain).\n- **rtl/ex_stage.sv** — instantiates `muldiv`, `ex_busy = m_op && !done`,\n  muldiv result muxed into `EX/MEM.alu_result`, new `bubble` input\n  (EX/MEM <= '0; dmem-stall hold keeps priority), exports forwarded rs1/rs2.\n- **rtl/hazard_unit.sv** — `ex_busy` ORed into `stall_if`/`stall_id`; new\n  `bubble_ex_mem = ex_busy && !dmem_stall`; `flush_if = imem_stall` only.\n- **rtl/if_stage.sv** — `redirect` removed from the IF/ID NOP mux *and*\n  from `out.valid` (item 6). Redirect acts only via the PC mux and\n  `flush_id`.\n- **rtl/core.sv** — wiring only. Top-level IO unchanged (nret=1).\n- **test/test_muldiv.py (new)** — every M-ext vector from test_alu.py\n  ported verbatim through the clocked handshake, plus back-to-back mixed\n  ops, result-held-until-ack, and a 46-vector corner/random sweep per op\n  against a Python RV32M reference (operand inputs are scrambled after the\n  capture cycle; exact latency asserted).\n- **test/test_alu.py** — RV32I vectors kept; M vectors moved; one test\n  pins that M encodings now fall to the ALU default.\n- **test/test_pipeline.py** — `muldiv.sv` added to sources; 5 new cases\n  (operands forwarded from EX/MEM + MEM/WB incl. RVFI rs*_rdata, result\n  consumed immediately, M-op behind a load, back-to-back MUL/DIV/REM incl.\n  div/rem by zero, wrong-path M-op after a taken branch).\n\n## Deviations from the hypothesis plan\n\n1. **MUL is 1 extra cycle, not 2.** I first built the contract's 2-extra-\n   cycle version (registered operands + registered product) and measured\n   it: `make timing` = 60.25 MHz, worst path MEM/WB.rd -> forward_unit ->\n   ALU -> dmem address, multiplier not in the top 5. The contract allows\n   cutting to 1 extra cycle in exactly that case, so I dropped the product\n   register: 62.39 MHz, 538 FFs (was 603), worst path now regfile -> EX\n   branch compare -> redirect -> ID/EX. Both numbers are placement\n   option 0 only (single run each); the evaluator takes the median of 3\n   options, so the ~2 MHz difference is within P&R noise — the claim is\n   only \"not slower\", plus one fewer cycle per MUL.\n2. **ALTOPS latency is 1 extra cycle, not the fixed 2** — it follows the\n   multiplier path so the formal model and the real MUL share one FSM path.\n3. **No `busy` output on muldiv** (unused by ex_stage; an unconnected pin\n   is a `-Wall` lint warning). No separate `result_q` register: the divide\n   result lives in `quo_q`, the multiply result is muxed from the product.\n4. **`out.valid` is no longer gated by `redirect`** (the hypothesis said it\n   \"may still be\"). It is redundant: on redirect ID/EX is either zeroed by\n   `flush_id` or held by dmem stall, never loaded.\n5. `op` is the 5-bit `alu_op` (decoded into flags at capture), not funct3.\n\n## Verification status (all on the final 1-extra-cycle RTL unless noted)\n\n- `verilator --lint-only -Wall`: clean.\n- cocotb (`pytest cores/bench/test`): 6/6 runners pass; test_muldiv 25/25,\n  test_pipeline 16/16.\n- `make cosim` (run as `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`): passed, 2 ELFs\n  (selftest with/without stalls + CoreMark CRCs). Plain `make cosim`\n  fails to *build* here because the Makefile's `cosim-build` prerequisite\n  defaults to NRET=2 while this core is nret=1 — pre-existing, unrelated\n  to this change; `tools.eval.cosim` sets NRET itself.\n- `bash formal/run_all.sh` (nret=1 auto-detect, ALTOPS):\n  - 2-extra-cycle version: **53 passed, 0 failed**.\n  - final 1-extra-cycle version: see \"Formal re-run\" below.\n- `make timing TARGET=bench` (Gowin, place option 0): baseline 5.44 MHz /\n  12312 LUT4 -> **62.39 MHz, 2381 logic, 538 FF, 2 DSP**.\n\n## Concerns\n\n- Fmax landed at ~60 MHz at option 0, above the hypothesis's 45-50 MHz\n  estimate, but it is one placement seed; not the scored median.\n- CoreMark iterations/cycle was not measured locally (cosim only checks\n  CRCs/RVFI), so the predicted ~1-3% cycle cost is unverified here.\n- `make formal-deep` (non-ALTOPS, proves the real multiplier/divider) was\n  not run — too slow for the 30-minute budget, and a 35-cycle divide\n  cannot retire inside a 20-step BMC anyway. Real arithmetic is covered by\n  test_muldiv.py and cosim only.\n- The DSP now has input registers but no output register; if a later\n  change shortens the two current worst paths, operand reg -> DSP ->\n  EX/MEM may become the limiter and the product register (S_MUL state)\n  would need to come back.\n", "structuredPatch": [], "originalFile": null, "userModified": false}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01J19txV4uKaf59EEhhTRhqJ", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "config", "reason_type": "mode"}}]}
