{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChLdVhwDVqFEzq69bJ8X6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Nc7YEi8CyvCkqVfr6ECUvq","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/srv/hwebench/clones/claude-fable-5_2_xhigh-v2-rep1/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261123-003-r1s2/cores/bench/implementation_notes.md","old_string":"- Timing (`make timing TARGET=bench`): TIMING_PLACEHOLDER","new_string":"- Timing (Gowin, `python3 -m tools.eval.gowin bench --all-options`, and\n  the same flow on the baseline HEAD RTL for a like-for-like comparison):\n\n  | placement option | baseline HEAD | this change |\n  |------------------|---------------|-------------|\n  | 0                | 5.140 MHz     | 5.117 MHz   |\n  | 1                | 5.442 MHz     | 5.564 MHz   |\n  | 2                | 5.442 MHz     | 5.564 MHz   |\n  | **median**       | **5.442 MHz** | **5.564 MHz** |\n\n  The worst path is unchanged in kind: MEM/WB `rd` -> forward_unit ->\n  EX operand mux -> ALU divider -> EX/MEM `alu_result` (absorbed into the\n  bench dmem BSRAM address register), ~200 ns, 149-151 logic levels. No\n  predictor / fetch-steering logic appears in the reported worst paths.\n  The +2.2% median Fmax is placement noise, not a property of the change.\n  Area: logic 12312 -> 12246, registers 460 -> 463, LUT-RAM 8 -> 24 (the\n  16 extra cells are the 256x2 counter table, inferred as distributed RAM\n  as intended), BSRAM/DSP unchanged.\n- Expected fitness from the two numbers above: iterations/cycle x1.071,\n  median Fmax x1.022 (noise) -> roughly +7% from the hypothesis itself,\n  about +9.5% as measured locally."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":875,"cache_read_input_tokens":139911,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":875},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier