{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChLdWXFZkGGVgNBZaR1V1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fetch-cycle branch predictor is implemented in `cores/bench/rtl/` and passes every local gate, with CoreMark iterations/cycle up 7.1% and no Fmax cost.\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Verilator lint (`-Wall`) | clean |\n| riscv-formal (nret=1 wrapper) | 53 passed, 0 failed, first attempt |\n| Cosim (selftest with/without stalls, CoreMark CRCs) | passed |\n| cocotb unit tests | all pass, including 7 new predictor tests and 3 new pipeline tests |\n| CoreMark cycles, `--istall --dstall` | 4,491,485 → 4,193,173 |\n| Gowin Fmax, median of 3 placements | 5.442 → 5.564 MHz |\n\n- **Fmax:** the worst path is still the EX divider at about 200 ns, so the +2.2% median Fmax is placement noise.\n- **Area:** the counter table is inferred as LUT-RAM (16 extra cells).\n\nDeviations from the plan:\n- **Counter carried down the pipeline:** the 2-bit counter read at fetch travels with the branch in ID/EX and is handed back at training, instead of being re-read at the EX index. This keeps the table to one read port and one write port. The only behavioural difference is a stale update when a branch's immediate predecessor in EX maps to the same entry (e.g. a branch-to-self).\n- **Reserved branch encodings:** funct3 2/3 are excluded in the fetch pre-decode, so an illegal branch is never steered.\n- **Table start state:** there is no `initial` block, so counters start at 0 rather than weakly-not-taken.\n\n`make formal TARGET=bench` and plain `make cosim TARGET=bench` fail on this nret=1 core before reaching the RTL, because they select the dual-channel wrapper and `NRET=2`. I ran the single-issue equivalents instead: `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh` and `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`.\n\nNotes are in `cores/bench/implementation_notes.md` (the gitignored path) rather than the worktree root, where the file would have shown up as untracked. Only `cores/bench/rtl/` and `cores/bench/test/test_*.py` show in `git status`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1589,"cache_read_input_tokens":140786,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1589},"output_tokens":812,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"efc18fa1-a986-416f-b405-8ea1312d06ca","uuid":"0f5eda96-3362-49bf-8a89-999c91a7cbd6","timestamp":"2026-11-23T22:14:31.044Z","request_id":"req_011ChLdWX7NKEPPk1Gr4zx4B"}
