{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01VepcZ2adTuXSRoP73UWfh3", "type": "tool_result", "content": "/srv/hwebench/clones/claude-fable-5_2_xhigh-v2-rep1/cores/bench\nard -> EX branch resolve -> redirect ->\\nhazard/flush -> ID/EX, untouched by this change. Keep the divider's\\nstart/busy logic off that path: derive div_busy from registered ID/EX\\nctrl bits and the divider's own FSM state only.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 50, \"confidence\": \"high\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/divider.sv\", \"description\": \"New sequential radix-2 restoring divider (start/busy/done handshake, operand latch, sign fix-up, RV32M div-by-zero/overflow semantics, short-latency ALTOPS variant under `ifdef RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS`).\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU arms (result now comes from divider.sv); replace the three 64-bit multipliers with one signed 33x33 multiplier whose 66-bit product serves MUL/MULH/MULHSU/MULHU. Keep ALTOPS branch consistent.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Instantiate divider; start it on a valid div op in ID/EX using forwarded operands; export div_busy; mux divider result into EX/MEM.alu_result; write a bubble into EX/MEM while busy (unless dmem stall holds it); use latched operands for rs1_val/rs2_val of the divide.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add div_busy input: hold PC and ID/EX (stall_if/stall_id) while the divider runs, without flushing ID/EX; keep redirect/dmem_stall priorities intact.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire div_busy from ex_stage to hazard_unit.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add an is_div (and optionally is_mul) decode bit to ctrl_t if needed so EX does not have to re-decode alu_op on the stall path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Drive the new is_div ctrl bit for funct7=0000001, funct3[2]=1 R-type ops (illegal-default discipline unchanged).\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Pass the new ctrl bit(s) through the ID/EX register.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Adapt M-extension vectors: MUL* stay combinational ALU checks; DIV/REM \n…[3046 of 6118 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:b26add0fbd8b5c12]…\n null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-23T22:19:43.456160Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 1, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-11-23 hyp-20261123-001-r1s0 (regression, +748.76%): Replacing the combinational `/`/`%` in alu.sv with a stalled multi-cycle radix-2 divider passed all gates and alone gave ~8.5x (that divider was the whole ~200 ns period), yet it lost the round to sibling hyp-20261123-002-r1s1 (+1039%), which did the same plus the two things this one deliberately left alone \\u2014 registering the 33x33 multiplier (MUL +1 cycle) and taking `redirect` off the if_stage NOP mux -> load-use compare -> ID/EX-enable path (not measured separately); the probe conclusion \\\"deleting the multiplier doesn't raise Fmax, so MUL is not the next bottleneck\\\" was a misread, because once the dominant path is gone the remaining ~25 ns EX paths are co-critical and mask each other, so a single-seed delete-one-block probe can't rank them and they have to be cut together.\"}\n\nhyp-20261123-002-r1s1.yaml\nhyp-20261123-003-r1s2.yaml", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "d55f0dbd-27d2-4ad1-ae4e-feeaf180c4a8", "uuid": "0f5b7a61-08da-4cb0-b326-485adf0e937e", "timestamp": "2026-11-23T22:21:39.062Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "/srv/hwebench/clones/claude-fable-5_2_xhigh-v2-rep1/cores/bench\nard -> EX branch resolve -> redirect ->\\nhazard/flush -> ID/EX, untouched by this change. Keep the divider's\\nstart/busy logic off that path: derive div_busy from registered ID/EX\\nctrl bits and the divider's own FSM state only.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 50, \"confidence\": \"high\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/divider.sv\", \"description\": \"New sequential radix-2 restoring divider (start/busy/done handshake, operand latch, sign fix-up, RV32M div-by-zero/overflow semantics, short-latency ALTOPS variant under `ifdef RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS`).\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU arms (result now comes from divider.sv); replace the three 64-bit multipliers with one signed 33x33 multiplier whose 66-bit product serves MUL/MULH/MULHSU/MULHU. Keep ALTOPS branch consistent.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Instantiate divider; start it on a valid div op in ID/EX using forwarded operands; export div_busy; mux divider result into EX/MEM.alu_result; write a bubble into EX/MEM while busy (unless dmem stall holds it); use latched operands for rs1_val/rs2_val of the divide.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add div_busy input: hold PC and ID/EX (stall_if/stall_id) while the divider runs, without flushing ID/EX; keep redirect/dmem_stall priorities intact.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire div_busy from ex_stage to hazard_unit.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add an is_div (and optionally is_mul) decode bit to ctrl_t if needed so EX does not have to re-decode alu_op on the stall path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Drive the new is_div ctrl bit for funct7=0000001, funct3[2]=1 R-type ops (illegal-default discipline unchanged).\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Pass the new ctrl bit(s) through the ID/EX register.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Adapt M-extension vectors: MUL* stay combinational ALU checks; DIV/REM \n…[3046 of 6118 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:b26add0fbd8b5c12]…\n null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-23T22:19:43.456160Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 1, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-1