{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_018BW7FvvTyhUj8P4ofJAG4W", "type": "tool_result", "content": "generated:\ntotal 40\ndrwxrwx---+ 5 nobody nogroup 4096 Nov 23 22:59 .\ndrwxrwx---+ 9 nobody nogroup 4096 Nov 23 23:21 ..\ndrwxrwx---+ 4 nobody nogroup 4096 Nov 23 22:59 gowin_p0\ndrwxrwx---+ 4 nobody nogroup 4096 Nov 23 22:59 gowin_p1\ndrwxrwx---+ 4 nobody nogroup 4096 Nov 23 22:59 gowin_p2\n\nworktrees:\ntotal 24\ndrwxrwx---+ 3 nobody    nogroup   4096 Nov 23 23:19 .\ndrwxrwx---+ 9 nobody    nogroup   4096 Nov 23 23:21 ..\ndrwxr-x---+ 2 hwebench3 hwebench3 4096 Nov 23 23:18 .claude\n     branches, since both now live in muldiv.sv and must stay consistent).\n  6. Shorten co-critical path (b): redirect and load_use_hazard are mutually\n     exclusive (both are functions of the SAME ID/EX instruction: redirect\n     needs is_branch/is_jump, load-use needs mem_read), and on redirect\n     flush_id already zeroes ID/EX with priority over stall. So if_stage\n     must stop muxing the IF/ID instruction with NOP on `redirect`: keep the\n     NOP mux for imem_stall only (imem_ready is a flop) and let redirect act\n     only through flush_id and the PC mux. hazard_unit then sees raw\n     instr[19:15]/[24:20] and redirect no longer feeds decode/regfile-read/\n     load-use logic. out.valid may still be gated by redirect.\n  Invariants untouched: decoder legality, rvfi_order (+1 per valid MEM/WB),\n  trap discipline, top-level IO, nret=1.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 50\n  confidence: high\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/muldiv.sv\n    description: \"New sequential M-extension unit: start/busy/done FSM, radix-2 restoring divider (~34 cycles), single 33x33 signed multiplier with registered operands and product, result_q register; ALTOPS branch with the same handshake and fixed 2-cycle latency.\"\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Remove the combinational MUL*/DIV*/REM* arms (real and ALTOPS); ALU becomes RV32I-only add/sub/logic/compare/shift/LUI.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add ctrl_t.is_muldiv (decoded M-op flag) so EX/hazard logic does not decode alu_op.\"\n  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n    description: \"Set is_muldiv inside the already-validated funct7==0000001 R-type arm only; is_illegal default and legality rules unchanged.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Pass is_muldiv into ID/EX; when ID/EX holds (stall && !flush) refresh rs1_val/rs2_val with the post-forward EX operands so a waiting M-op keeps correct operands and RVFI rs*_rdata after its producers retire.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Instantiate muldiv, start it on the first EX cycle of an M-op with forwarded operands, mux result_q into EX/MEM.alu_result, export ex_busy and the forwarded rs1/rs2; add bubble input that loads EX/MEM with '0 while busy (hold on dmem stall keeps priority).\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Add ex_busy input: OR into stall_if/stall_id, emit bubble_ex_mem = ex_busy && !dmem_stall.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Remove `redirect` from the IF/ID instruction NOP mux (NOP only on imem stall); redirect keeps PC priority and kills the wrong-path instruction via flush_id only. Cuts the redirect -> NOP mux -> load-use compare -> ID/EX enable path.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire ex_busy/bubble_ex_mem and the forwarded-operand refresh between ex_stage, id_stage and hazard_unit.\"\n  - file: test/test_muldiv.py\n    description: \"New cocotb suite for muldiv: every M-ext vector currently in test_alu.py ported unchanged (30+ per op, div-by-zero, INT_MIN/-1, back-to-back ops) but driven through the clocked start/done handshake.\"\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: \"Keep the RV32I ALU vectors on the combinational alu; M-ext vectors move verbatim to test_muldiv.py (no vector dropped, invariant 5b coverage preserved).\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Add pipeline cases: M-op whose operands are forwarded from EX/MEM and MEM/WB, M-op followed immediately by a consumer, M-op behind a load, back-to-back MUL/DIV; fix any fixed-latency assumptions.\"", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "d55f0dbd-27d2-4ad1-ae4e-feeaf180c4a8", "uuid": "b9705936-40b2-46b8-9e1f-2193291cfe0a", "timestamp": "2026-11-23T22:21:48.314Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "generated:\ntotal 40\ndrwxrwx---+ 5 nobody nogroup 4096 Nov 23 22:59 .\ndrwxrwx---+ 9 nobody nogroup 4096 Nov 23 23:21 ..\ndrwxrwx---+ 4 nobody nogroup 4096 Nov 23 22:59 gowin_p0\ndrwxrwx---+ 4 nobody nogroup 4096 Nov 23 22:59 gowin_p1\ndrwxrwx---+ 4 nobody nogroup 4096 Nov 23 22:59 gowin_p2\n\nworktrees:\ntotal 24\ndrwxrwx---+ 3 nobody    nogroup   4096 Nov 23 23:19 .\ndrwxrwx---+ 9 nobody    nogroup   4096 Nov 23 23:21 ..\ndrwxr-x---+ 2 hwebench3 hwebench3 4096 Nov 23 23:18 .claude\n     branches, since both now live in muldiv.sv and must stay consistent).\n  6. Shorten co-critical path (b): redirect and load_use_hazard are mutually\n     exclusive (both are functions of the SAME ID/EX instruction: redirect\n     needs is_branch/is_jump, load-use needs mem_read), and on redirect\n     flush_id already zeroes ID/EX with priority over stall. So if_stage\n     must stop muxing the IF/ID instruction with NOP on `redirect`: keep the\n     NOP mux for imem_stall only (imem_ready is a flop) and let redirect act\n     only through flush_id and the PC mux. hazard_unit then sees raw\n     instr[19:15]/[24:20] and redirect no longer feeds decode/regfile-read/\n     load-use logic. out.valid may still be gated by redirect.\n  Invariants untouched: decoder legality, rvfi_order (+1 per valid MEM/WB),\n  trap discipline, top-level IO, nret=1.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 50\n  confidence: high\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/muldiv.sv\n    description: \"New sequential M-extension unit: start/busy/done FSM, radix-2 restoring divider (~34 cycles), single 33x33 signed multiplier with