{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_014wEVSKe4eXvjV3dG3MAAvH", "type": "tool_result", "content": "===== Write branch_predictor.sv\n// rtl/branch_predictor.sv\n//\n// Bimodal direction predictor: 2**IDX_BITS two-bit saturating counters.\n//\n//   - Fetch-side lookup is asynchronous (rd_idx = fetch pc[IDX_BITS+1:2]);\n//     rd_taken = counter MSB.\n//   - EX-side training is synchronous. The counter value that was read at\n//     fetch travels down the pipeline with the branch (if_id_t / id_ex_t\n//     .pred_ctr) and comes back on upd_ctr, so the table needs exactly ONE\n//     read port and ONE write port — the canonical distributed-RAM\n//     (LUT-RAM) shape. The saturating +1 / -1 is applied here.\n//   - The array has no reset on purpose (keeps it inferable as LUT-RAM).\n//     Contents are prediction-only: every prediction is verified in EX, so\n//     ANY table state is functionally safe (formal runs with it symbolic).\n//\n// Latency:        lookup combinational; update visible the cycle after\n//                 upd_en.\n// RVFI fields:    none (affects only how many cycles a retirement takes).\nmodule branch_predictor #(\n  parameter IDX_BITS = 8\n) (\n  input  logic                clock,\n  // fetch-side lookup\n  input  logic [IDX_BITS-1:0] rd_idx,\n  output logic [1:0]          rd_ctr,\n  output logic                rd_taken,\n  // EX-side training\n  input  logic                upd_en,\n  input  logic [IDX_BITS-1:0] upd_idx,\n  input  logic [1:0]          upd_ctr,    // counter value seen at fetch\n  input  logic                upd_taken   // resolved direction\n);\n\n  logic [1:0] ctr_mem [0:(1<<IDX_BITS)-1];\n  logic [1:0] upd_next;\n\n  always_comb begin\n    if (upd_taken) upd_next = (upd_ctr == 2'b11) ? 2'b11 : (upd_ctr + 2'b01);\n    else           upd_next = (upd_ctr == 2'b00) ? 2'b00 : (upd_ctr - 2'b01);\n  end\n\n  always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\n    if (upd_en) ctr_mem[upd_idx] <= upd_next;\n  end\n\n  assign rd_ctr   = ctr_mem[rd_idx];\n  assign rd_taken = rd_ctr[1];\n\nendmodule\n\n===== Write if_stage.sv\n// rtl/if_stage.sv\n//\n// Instruction fetch stage. Holds the PC register; the IF/ID payload\n// (pc + instr + valid + prediction) \n…[10096 of 13168 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:db5ad18e06519e85]…\n| baseline HEAD | this change |\n  |------------------|---------------|-------------|\n  | 0                | 5.140 MHz     | 5.117 MHz   |\n  | 1                | 5.442 MHz     | 5.564 MHz   |\n  | 2                | 5.442 MHz     | 5.564 MHz   |\n  | **median**       | **5.442 MHz** | **5.564 MHz** |\n\n  The worst path is unchanged in kind: MEM/WB `rd` -> forward_unit ->\n  EX operand mux -> ALU divider -> EX/MEM `alu_result` (absorbed into the\n  bench dmem BSRAM address register), ~200 ns, 149-151 logic levels. No\n  predictor / fetch-steering logic appears in the reported worst paths.\n  The +2.2% median Fmax is placement noise, not a property of the change.\n  Area: logic 12312 -> 12246, registers 460 -> 463, LUT-RAM 8 -> 24 (the\n  16 extra cells are the 256x2 counter table, inferred as distributed RAM\n  as intended), BSRAM/DSP unchanged.\n- Expected fitness from the two numbers above: iterations/cycle x1.071,\n  median Fmax x1.022 (noise) -> roughly +7% from the hypothesis itself,\n  about +9.5% as measured locally.", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "56a9f7e4-f52e-40a5-a6f8-de4bf29d2f35", "uuid": "01c6764c-83a2-4182-a581-cea54397beb8", "timestamp": "2026-11-23T22:25:11.571Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "===== Write branch_predictor.sv\n// rtl/branch_predictor.sv\n//\n// Bimodal direction predictor: 2**IDX_BITS two-bit saturating counters.\n//\n//   - Fetch-side lookup is asynchronous (rd_idx = fetch pc[IDX_BITS+1:2]);\n//     rd_taken = counter MSB.\n//   - EX-side training is synchronous. The counter value that was read at\n//     fetch travels down the pipeline with the branch (if_id_t / id_e