{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-fable-5-2", "id": "msg_011ChLcZNLkD4FmQUpysxfVp", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_011V72fDv8rE4HPtgVJdok8J", "name": "Write", "input": {"file_path": "/srv/hwebench/clones/claude-fable-5_2_xhigh-v2-rep1/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261123-001-r1s0-hypgen/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261123-001-r1s0.yaml", "content": "id: hyp-20261123-001-r1s0\ntitle: \"Multi-cycle iterative divider + single 33x33 multiplier: take DIV/REM off the EX critical path\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  Fmax is 5.44 MHz because the worst path (199.8 ns, 156 cells) runs\n  forward_unit -> ex_stage operand mux -> alu -> EX/MEM register through the\n  purely combinational 32-bit `/` and `%` operators in alu.sv (four of them:\n  signed/unsigned quotient and remainder). Everything else in the 5-stage\n  pipeline is an order of magnitude shorter. CoreMark executes almost no\n  DIV/REM instructions, so the whole clock period is being set by an\n  operation that is practically never used. The same alu.sv also builds three\n  separate 64x64-bit multipliers (mul_ss, mul_uu, mul_su with 64-bit\n  sign-extended operands) where one 33x33 signed multiplier is sufficient;\n  once the divider is gone those become the next-longest EX path and they\n  also waste DSP blocks / LUTs (12.3k LUT4 today vs. a 10k target).\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the combinational divider with a sequential radix-2 restoring\n  divider that iterates one quotient bit per clock while the pipeline is\n  stalled, and collapse the three multipliers into one.\n\n  Divider (new rtl/divider.sv, instantiated in ex_stage):\n    - Start when ID/EX holds a valid DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU and the unit is idle.\n      On the start cycle latch the *forwarded* rs1/rs2 (and op), because the\n      EX/MEM and MEM/WB forwarding sources drain away while EX is held; the\n      latched values also feed EX/MEM.rs1_val/rs2_val/write_data for RVFI.\n    - Work on magnitudes: take |a|, |b| for DIV/REM, run 32 shift-subtract\n      steps on a {remainder, quotient} shift register with one 33-bit\n      subtractor, then conditionally negate (quotient if signs differ and\n      b != 0; remainder if dividend negative). This yields the RV32M corner\n      cases for free: x/0 -> all-ones quotient, remainder = dividend;\n      INT_MIN/-1 -> INT_MIN, remainder 0. ~34-35 cycles per divide.\n    - `div_busy` = valid div in ID/EX and result not yet done. While busy:\n      hazard_unit holds PC and ID/EX (stall_if/stall_id) and ex_stage writes\n      a bubble (valid=0, reg_write=0, mem_read=mem_write=0) into EX/MEM\n      unless dmem_stall is already holding EX/MEM. On the done cycle (and\n      only when EX/MEM is not held by dmem_stall) the instruction advances\n      with the divider result as alu_result; the FSM returns to idle exactly\n      when the instruction leaves EX. A redirect cannot originate from a\n      divide in EX, and a flush of ID/EX (reset) must reset the FSM.\n    - Under `RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS` the unit keeps the identical\n      start/busy/done handshake but returns the ALTOPS formula\n      ((a - b) ^ const) after a short fixed latency (1-2 cycles), so the\n      BMC depth budget and the liveness check still close while formal\n      proves the stall/forward/bubble behaviour of the new handshake.\n\n  Multiplier (rtl/alu.sv): build one signed 33x33 product\n    p = $signed({a_sx, a}) * $signed({b_sx, b})   (66 bits)\n  with a_sx = a[31] for MULH/MULHSU else 0 and b_sx = b[31] for MULH else 0;\n  MUL = p[31:0], MULH/MULHU/MULHSU = p[63:32]. Same results, one third of\n  the multiplier hardware, shorter EX path. MUL stays single-cycle so the\n  multiply-heavy CoreMark matrix kernel loses no IPC.\n\n  The divider case arms are removed from the combinational ALU case\n  statement; alu.sv keeps ALTOPS and real branches consistent.\n\n  Expected result: iterations/cycle unchanged to within <1% (DIV/REM are\n  vanishingly rare in CoreMark, each now costs ~34 extra cycles), while the\n  critical path drops from ~200 ns to the forward-mux -> multiplier/adder ->\n  EX/MEM path (a few tens of ns at worst), i.e. Fmax rises several-fold.\n  The real gain is expected to be far above the +50% schema ceiling.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 50\n  confidence: high\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/divider.sv\n    description: \"New sequential radix-2 restoring divider (start/busy/done handshake, operand latch, sign fix-up, RV32M div-by-zero/overflow semantics, short-latency ALTOPS variant under `ifdef RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS`).\"\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Remove combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU arms (result now comes from divider.sv); replace the three 64-bit multipliers with one signed 33x33 multiplier whose 66-bit product serves MUL/MULH/MULHSU/MULHU. Keep ALTOPS branch consistent.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Instantiate divider; start it on a valid div op in ID/EX using forwarded operands; export div_busy; mux divider result into EX/MEM.alu_result; write a bubble into EX/MEM while busy (unless dmem stall holds it); use latched operands for rs1_val/rs2_val of the divide.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Add div_busy input: hold PC and ID/EX (stall_if/stall_id) while the divider runs, without flushing ID/EX; keep redirect/dmem_stall priorities intact.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire div_busy from ex_stage to hazard_unit.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add an is_div (and optionally is_mul) decode bit to ctrl_t if needed so EX does not have to re-decode alu_op on the stall path.\"\n  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n    description: \"Drive the new is_div ctrl bit for funct7=0000001, funct3[2]=1 R-type ops (illegal-default discipline unchanged).\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Pass the new ctrl bit(s) through the ID/EX register.\"\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: \"Adapt M-extension vectors: MUL* stay combinational ALU checks; DIV/REM vectors (incl. div-by-zero and INT_MIN/-1) drive the sequential divider through its start/done handshake.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Add pipeline tests for DIV/REM with forwarded operands, back-to-back divides, divide followed by dependent instruction, and divides under imem/dmem stalls.\"\n"}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 6172, "cache_read_input_tokens": 51070, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 6172}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "f3f1fd54-c649-4ee3-88e7-d8244d8800ab", "uuid": "f717a84d-928c-425c-9f17-fa050753f5ff", "timestamp": "2026-11-23T22:02:21.036Z", "request_id": "req_011ChLcZN5cYVjQ1ZH9tSWzv"}
