{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01JB6B1oeGBnB3WDNWwLGQjX", "type": "tool_result", "content": "[options]\nisa rv32im\nnret 1\nsolver bitwuzla\n\n[depth]\n# BMC depth per check. 2nd column (where present) is the k-induction prove\n# depth. Keep depths matched to the current pipeline so bugs within ~20\n# cycles of any symbolic instruction stream are exposed.\ninsn          20\nreg       10  20\npc_fwd    10  20\npc_bwd    10  20\ncausal    10  20\n# unique   — no two retirements share rvfi_order (catches double-retire)\n# cover    — sanity that the CPU retires (prevents vacuous-pass suites)\n# ill      — illegal instructions must trap; rvfi_trap from decoder.is_illegal\n# liveness — CPU makes forward progress under any symbolic stream\nunique     1 10 20\ncover      1    20\nill             20\nliveness   1 10 20\n\n[defines]\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALIGNED_MEM\n# RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS — fast mode. Same as checks.cfg. See checks.cfg for\n# the full rationale on what ALTOPS does and does not prove. M-extension\n# arithmetic correctness is covered by test/test_alu.py and `make formal-deep`.\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\n\n[cover]\n# Sanity cover: the CPU must retire at least one non-trapping instruction.\nalways @* if (!reset) cover (rvfi_valid && !rvfi_trap);\n\n[verilog-files]\n# run_all.sh rebuilds this section from the actual rtl/ glob; the list\n# below is overwritten before genchecks runs. Kept as a placeholder so\n# the section is syntactically present for any reader inspecting the cfg.\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/core.sv\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/wrapper.sv\n3:The ALU is purely combinational (RV32IM). MUL / DIV / REM use the\n17:    ALU_DIV, ALU_DIVU, ALU_REM, ALU_REMU,\n43:async def _check_div(dut, op, a, b, expected):\n44:    \"\"\"Combinational div/rem — alias for _check. Was a multi-cycle FSM\n150:async def div_signed(dut):\n152:    await _check_div(dut, ALU_DIV, 10, 3, 3)\n153:    await _check_div(dut, ALU_DIV, 0xFFFFFFFC, 2, 0xFFFFFFFE)      # -4/2 = -2\n154:    await _check_div(dut, ALU_DIV, 7, 0xFFFFFFFE, 0xFFFFFFFD)      # 7/-2 = -3 (trunc to 0)\n158:async def div_by_zero(dut):\n160:    await _check_div(dut, ALU_DIV, 123, 0, 0xFFFFFFFF)\n161:    await _check_div(dut, ALU_DIV, 0, 0, 0xFFFFFFFF)\n165:async def div_overflow(dut):\n168:    await _check_div(dut, ALU_DIV, 0x80000000, 0xFFFFFFFF, 0x80000000)\n172:async def divu(dut):\n174:    await _check_div(dut, ALU_DIVU, 0xFFFFFFFF, 2, 0x7FFFFFFF)\n175:    await _check_div(dut, ALU_DIVU, 100, 7, 14)\n179:async def divu_by_zero(dut):\n181:    await _check_div(dut, ALU_DIVU, 42, 0, 0xFFFFFFFF)\n187:    await _check_div(dut, ALU_REM, 10, 3, 1)\n189:    await _check_div(dut, ALU_REM, 0xFFFFFFF6, 3, 0xFFFFFFFF)\n356", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "f3f1fd54-c649-4ee3-88e7-d8244d8800ab", "uuid": "91e826c4-0952-453d-814f-063840cf4089", "timestamp": "2026-11-23T22:02:55.191Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "[options]\nisa rv32im\nnret 1\nsolver bitwuzla\n\n[depth]\n# BMC depth per check. 2nd column (where present) is the k-induction prove\n# depth. Keep depths matched to the current pipeline so bugs within ~20\n# cycles of any symbolic instruction stream are exposed.\ninsn          20\nreg       10  20\npc_fwd    10  20\npc_bwd    10  20\ncausal    10  20\n# unique   — no two retirements share rvfi_order (catches double-retire)\n# cover    — sanity that the CPU retires (prevents vacuous-pass suites)\n# ill      — illegal instructions must trap; rvfi_trap from decoder.is_illegal\n# liveness — CPU makes forward progress under any symbolic stream\nunique     1 10 20\ncover      1    20\nill             20\nliveness   1 10 20\n\n[defines]\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALIGNED_MEM\n# RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS — fast mode. Same as checks.cfg. See checks.cfg for\n# the full rationale on what ALTOPS does and does not prove. M-extension\n# arithmetic correctness is covered by test/test_alu.py and `make formal-deep`.\n`define RI