{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChLd4MLXF1SrgMKwGmx7c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The hypothesis is written to `cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261123-001-r1s0.yaml` and validates against the schema.\n\n**Proposal (micro_opt):** replace the combinational divider with a multi-cycle iterative one that stalls the pipeline, and collapse the three 64-bit multipliers into one 33×33 signed multiplier that stays single-cycle.\n\n**Why:** the 199.8 ns worst path that pins Fmax at 5.44 MHz runs through the combinational `/` and `%` in `alu.sv`. The proposal assumes CoreMark executes almost no DIV/REM in the timed region, so iterations per cycle should barely move; I did not count them.\n\n**Timing probe:** I ran the Gowin flow (place option 0 only) on a scratch copy of the RTL with the divider arms deleted and the single multiplier in place. This approximates the proposal — it does not include the new divider or its stall logic, and it was not simulated.\n\n| Variant | Fmax | LUTs | DSP |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Baseline | 5.44 MHz | 12312 | — |\n| Divider removed, one 33×33 single-cycle multiplier | 49.41 MHz | 1971 | 2 |\n| Divider and multiplier both removed | 46.7 MHz | 1922 | 0 |\n\n- **Multiplier is not the next bottleneck:** removing it as well does not raise Fmax, so the hypothesis keeps MUL single-cycle and loses no CoreMark throughput.\n- **Remaining worst path:** about 25.5 ns, from the regfile through EX branch resolve, redirect and the hazard unit into the ID/EX register. This change does not touch it.\n- **Expected gain:** roughly 9× Fmax if the probe holds once the real divider is in. The YAML states `fitness_delta_pct: 50` with high confidence because 50 is the schema ceiling.\n\nThe YAML also specifies how the divider should latch forwarded operands, interact with dmem stalls, and behave under `RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS` (same handshake, short fixed latency) so the formal checks still close.\n\nThe worktree's RTL is untouched; the probe copies live under `$TMPDIR`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":225,"cache_read_input_tokens":75086,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":225},"output_tokens":763,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f3f1fd54-c649-4ee3-88e7-d8244d8800ab","uuid":"138f54a6-e73f-400d-b005-80a2e0f6ce5f","timestamp":"2026-11-23T22:08:36.597Z","request_id":"req_011ChLd4MCbDfAkaLS4zQxKG"}
