{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01TectJfXaqikbUkTq4vj8xb", "type": "tool_result", "content": "[options]\nisa rv32im\nnret 1\nsolver bitwuzla\n\n[depth]\n# BMC depth per check. 2nd column (where present) is the k-induction prove\n# depth. Keep depths matched to the current pipeline so bugs within ~20\n# cycles of any symbolic instruction stream are exposed.\ninsn          20\nreg       10  20\npc_fwd    10  20\npc_bwd    10  20\ncausal    10  20\n# unique   — no two retirements share rvfi_order (catches double-retire)\n# cover    — sanity that the CPU retires (prevents vacuous-pass suites)\n# ill      — illegal instructions must trap; rvfi_trap from decoder.is_illegal\n# liveness — CPU makes forward progress under any symbolic stream\nunique     1 10 20\ncover      1    20\nill             20\nliveness   1 10 20\n\n[defines]\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALIGNED_MEM\n# RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS — fast mode. Same as checks.cfg. See checks.cfg for\n# the full rationale on what ALTOPS does and does not prove. M-extension\n# arithmetic correctness is covered by test/test_alu.py and `make formal-deep`.\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\n\n[cover]\n# Sanity cover: the CPU must retire at least one non-trapping instruction.\nalways @* if (!reset) cover (rvfi_valid && !rvfi_trap);\n\n[verilog-files]\n# run_all.sh rebuilds this section from the actual rtl/ glob; the list\n# below is overwritten before genchecks runs. Kept as a placeholder so\n# the section is syntactically present for any reader inspecting the cfg.\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/core.sv\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/wrapper.sv\n----\n\"\"\"Unit tests for rtl/alu.sv.\n\nThe ALU is purely combinational (RV32IM). MUL / DIV / REM use the\nSystemVerilog `*`, `/`, `%` operators and resolve in zero cycles, so\nthere is no clock, reset, or handshake on this module.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport cocotb\nfrom cocotb.triggers import Timer\n\nfrom _helpers import (\n    ALU_ADD, ALU_SUB, ALU_AND, ALU_OR, ALU_XOR,\n    ALU_SLT, ALU_SLTU, ALU_SLL, ALU_SRL, ALU_SRA,\n    ALU_LUI,\n    ALU_MUL, ALU_MULH, ALU_MULHU, ALU_MULHSU,\n    ALU_DIV, ALU_DIVU, ALU_REM, ALU_REMU,\n    run_cocotb,\n)\n\nMASK32 = 0xFFFFFFFF\n\n\nasync def _setup(dut):\n  \n…[3109 of 6181 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:85d2c2ceff16ec7d]…\noplevel: str, sources: list[str], test_module: str) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Build the DUT under Verilator and run the given cocotb test_module.\n\n    `sources` is a list of bare filenames under rtl/. Order matters —\n    package files (e.g. core_pkg.sv) come first.\n    \"\"\"\n    sim = os.environ.get(\"SIM\", \"verilator\")\n    runner = get_runner(sim)\n    build_dir = SIM_BUILD / toplevel\n\n    runner.build(\n----\n11:#   default: formal/checks.cfg       (fast, ALTOPS, used by orchestrator)\n12:#   deep   : formal/checks-deep.cfg  (no ALTOPS, proves M-ext arithmetic)\n26:  echo \"  Example: RTL_DIR=cores/v1/rtl CORE_NAME=v1 bash formal/run_all.sh formal/checks.cfg\" >&2\n150:# Stage rtl + wrapper + the chosen checks config under the framework's\n155:# deletes a module in rtl/ leaves a ghost copy in $CORE_DIR from the\n158:# right to rename/delete files in rtl/, so this cleanup is required.\n163:# Stage checks.cfg with [verilog-files] auto-derived from actual rtl/\n167:# files in rtl/. Hardcoding silently fails on those restructurings (or", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "1ef5e113-78fa-45f5-9d31-b22c88a410f8", "uuid": "7e24f074-4b21-4d9e-9b03-1074742453e8", "timestamp": "2026-11-23T22:02:25.938Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "[options]\nisa rv32im\nnret 1\nsolver bitwuzla\n\n[depth]\n# BMC depth per check. 2nd column (where present) is the k-induction prove\n# depth. Keep depths matched to the current pipeline so bugs within ~20\n# cycles of any symbolic instruction stream are exposed.\ninsn          20\nreg       10  20\npc_fwd    10  20\npc_bwd    10  20\ncausal    10  20\n# unique   — n