, " motivation: |", "   Fmax is 5.44 MHz because the worst path (199.8 ns, 150 logic levels) runs", "-  MEM/WB.rd -> forward_unit -> EX operand mux -> alu.sv combinational", "-  32-bit `/` and `%` -> EX/MEM.alu_result -> dmem address. The single-cycle", "-  divider (four of them: DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU, signed and unsigned) is also why", "-  the core costs 12.3k LUT4. Three separate 64-bit combinational multipliers", "-  (mul_ss/mul_uu/mul_su, 6 DSPs) sit in the same forward->ALU->EX/MEM loop", "-  and would be the next limiter. CoreMark executes almost no divides and", "-  only a few percent multiplies, so making these ops multi-cycle costs", "-  ~1-3% cycles while the clock can rise by roughly an order of magnitude.", "+  MEM/WB.rd -> forward_unit -> EX operand mux -> alu.sv combinational 32-bit", "+  `/` and `%` -> EX/MEM.alu_result (= dmem BSRAM address). The single-cycle", "+  dividers are also why the core is 12.3k LUT4 with only 460 FFs. Three", "+  separate 64-bit combinational multipliers (mul_ss/mul_uu/mul_su, 6 DSPs)", "+  sit in the same forward -> ALU -> EX/MEM loop and are the next limiter once", "+  the divider is gone. CoreMark's timed region executes essentially no", "+  divides and only a few percent multiplies, so making these ops multi-cycle", "+  costs ~1-3% cycles (CoreMark/MHz stays ~2.15-2.2) while the clock period", "+  can drop by an order of magnitude. Nothing else in the design is within", "+  10x of this path, so every other optimisation is invisible until this", "+  structural change lands.", " hypothesis: |", "-  Remove multiply/divide from the combinational ALU and execute them in a", "-  sequential M-unit that stalls the pipeline through a busy/done handshake.", "-  Everything else in EX stays single-cycle, so the EX loop shrinks to", "-  forward-mux -> 32-bit add/shift/compare -> EX/MEM (expected 10-14 ns", "-  instead of 200 ns; Fmax 60-90 MHz vs 5.4 MHz). With CoreMark/MHz staying", "-  near 2.1-2.2 the fitness should land far above +50% (roughly 10x).", "+  Take multiply/divide out of the single-cycle EX path. A new sequential", "+  M-unit (rtl/muldiv.sv) executes them over several cycles while the M", "+  instruction waits in ID/EX; EX/MEM receives bubbles until the result is", "+  registered. All RV32I ops stay single-cycle, so the EX loop becomes", "+  forward-mux -> 32-bit add/shift/compare -> EX/MEM. Expected Fmax 55-90 MHz", "+  (vs 5.44), fitness roughly 120-190 iter/s, i.e. far beyond the +50% the", "+  schema field can express.", "+", "+  Design contract for the implementer:", "+  1. muldiv.sv, ports: clock, reset, start, op, a, b -> busy/done, result.", "+     - Divider: radix-2 restoring, 1 bit/cycle on magnitudes (setup cycle", "+       takes |a|,|b| and records signs; 32 iterate cycles of a 33-bit", "+       subtract + shift; final cycle applies sign fix into result_q).", "+       RV32M corner cases fall out of the algorithm with one rule: negate", "+       the quotient only if signs differ AND b != 0 (div-by-0 -> all ones,", "+       rem-by-0 -> dividend, INT_MIN/-1 -> INT_MIN, rem 0). No early-out", "+       needed: divides are not on CoreMark's timed path.", "+     - Multiplier: ONE 33x33 signed multiply (operand sign bits =", "+       a[31]&a_signed, b[31]&b_signed) replacing the three 64-bit ones.", "+       Operands are registered (DSP input regs), product registered", "+       (DSP output reg), result_q = op==MUL ? p[31:0] : p[63:32].", "+       Start with 2 extra cycles; cut to 1 extra cycle only if", "+       `make timing` shows reg -> DSP -> EX/MEM is not the worst path.", "+     - Under `ifdef RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS` keep the SAME FSM/handshake but", "+       compute the ALTOPS formulas from the captured operands with a fixed", "+       2-cycle latency. Required: insn checks are 20-step BMC and liveness", "+       allows ~10 cycles between retirements, so a 34-cycle divide cannot", "+       retire inside the window. Real latency is covered by cosim + cocotb.", "+  2. ex_stage.sv: m_op = in.valid && ctrl.is_muldiv (new decoded ctrl bit so", "+     EX does not compare alu_op). start = m_op && FSM idle, operands = the", "+     post-forward rs1/rs2. ex_busy = m_op && !done. When done, EX/MEM", "+     captures result_q through the existing alu_result mux; the FSM returns", "+     to idle on the cycle EX/MEM actually captures (!stall_ex_mem).", "+  3. hazard_unit.sv: stall_if |= ex_busy; stall_id |= ex_busy; new output", "+     bubble_ex_mem = ex_busy && !dmem_stall (EX/MEM <= '0). dmem_stall keeps", "+     priority (EX/MEM holds, M-unit keeps iterating or waits in DONE). An", "+     M-op in EX is never a load or branch, so load_use/redirect/flush_id", "+     cannot fire against it.", "+  4. Operand staleness (the classic bug): while the M-op waits in EX its", "+     producers drain out of EX/MEM and MEM/WB, so ID/EX.rs?_val would be", "+     stale at the done cycle (wrong rvfi_rs?_rdata, and wrong operands if", "+     start were late). Fix in id_stage.sv: whenever ID/EX holds (stall &&", "+     !flush) write the post-forward rs1/rs2 back into ID/EX.rs1_val/rs2_val.", "+     Forwarding is then correct on every held cycle by induction, and", "+     EX/MEM.rs1_val/rs2_val are right when the M-op finally moves.", "+  5. alu.sv keeps only RV32I ops (M arms deleted in both the ALTOPS and real", "+     branches, since both now live in muldiv.sv and must stay consistent).", "+  Invariants untouched: decoder legality, rvfi_order (+1 per valid MEM/WB),", "+  trap discipline, top-level IO, nret=1.", " expected_impact:", "   fitness_delta_pct: 50", "   confidence: high", " changes:", "   - file: rtl/muldiv.sv", "-    description: \"New sequential M-extension unit (start/busy/done handshake): iterative radix-2 restoring divider and a registered-operand, registered-product single 33x33 signed multiplier.\"", "+    description: \"New sequential M-extension unit: start/busy/done FSM, radix-2 restoring divider (~34 cycles), single 33x33 signed multiplier with registered operands and product, result_q register; ALTOPS branch with the same handshake and fixed 2-cycle latency.\"", "   - file: rtl/alu.sv", "-    description: \"Drop the combinational MUL*/DIV*/REM* arms; keep the RV32I ops only.\"", "+    description: \"Remove the combinational MUL*/DIV*/REM* arms (real and ALTOPS); ALU becomes RV32I-only add/sub/logic/compare/shift/LUI.\"", "+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv", "+    description: \"Add ctrl_t.is_muldiv (decoded M-op flag) so EX/hazard logic does not decode alu_op.\"", "+  - file: rtl/decoder.sv", "+    description: \"Set is_muldiv inside the already-validated funct7==0000001 R-type arm only; is_illegal default and legality rules unchanged.\"", "+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv", "+    description: \"Pass is_muldiv into ID/EX; when ID/EX holds (stall && !flush) refresh rs1_val/rs2_val with the post-forward EX operands so a waiting M-op keeps correct operands and RVFI rs*_rdata after its producers retire.\"", "   - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv", "-    description: \"Instantiate muldiv, start it for M-ops, select its result into EX/MEM.alu_result, export ex_busy.\"", "+    description: \"Instantiate muldiv, start it on the first EX cycle of an M-op with forwarded operands, mux result_q into EX/MEM.alu_result, export ex_busy and the forwarded rs1/rs2; add bubble input that loads EX/MEM with '0 while busy (hold on dmem stall keeps priority).\"", "   - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv", "-    description: \"Add ex_busy stall: hold PC and ID/EX, insert bubble into EX/MEM while the M-unit is running.\"", "+    description: \"Add ex_busy input: OR into stall_if/stall_id, emit bubble_ex_mem = ex_busy && !dmem_stall.\"", "   - file: rtl/core.sv", "-    description: \"Wire ex_busy between ex_stage and hazard_unit.\"", "+    description: \"Wire ex_busy/bubble_ex_mem and the forwarded-operand refresh between ex_stage, id_stage and hazard_unit.\"", "   - file: test/test_muldiv.py", "-    description: \"Cocotb unit test for the sequential M-unit with the RV32M corner vectors.\"", "+    description: \"New cocotb suite for muldiv: every M-ext vector currently in test_alu.py ported unchanged (30+ per op, div-by-zero, INT_MIN/-1, back-to-back ops) but driven through the clocked start/done handshake.\"", "+  - file: test/test_alu.py", "+    description: \"Keep the RV32I ALU vectors on the combinational alu; M-ext vectors move verbatim to test_muldiv.py (no vector dropped, invariant 5b coverage preserved).\"", "+  - file: test/test_pipeline.py", "+    description: \"Add pipeline cases: M-op whose operands are forwarded from EX/MEM and MEM/WB, M-op followed immediately by a consumer, M-op behind a load, back-to-back MUL/DIV; fix any fixed-latency assumptions.\""]}], "originalFile": "id: hyp-20261123-002-r1s1\ntitle: \"Multi-cycle M-unit: iterative divider + 2-stage DSP multiplier with EX-stall handshake\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  Fmax is 5.44 MHz because the worst path (199.8 ns, 150 logic levels) runs\n  MEM/WB.rd -> forward_unit -> EX operand mux -> alu.sv combinational\n  32-bit `/` and `%` -> EX/MEM.alu_result -> dmem address. The single-cycle\n  divider (four of them: DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU, signed and unsigned) is also why\n  the core costs 12.3k LUT4. Three separate 64-bit combinational multipliers\n  (mul_ss/mul_uu/mul_su, 6 DSPs) sit in the same forward->ALU->EX/MEM loop\n  and would be the next limiter. CoreMark executes almost no divides and\n  only a few percent multiplies, so making these ops multi-cycle costs\n  ~1-3% cycles while the clock can rise by roughly an order of magnitude.\nhypothesis: |\n  Remove multiply/divide from the combinational ALU and execute them in a\n  sequential M-unit that stalls the pipeline through a busy/done handshake.\n  Everything else in EX stays single-cycle, so the EX loop shrinks to\n  forward-mux -> 32-bit add/shift/compare -> EX/MEM (expected 10-14 ns\n  instead of 200 ns; Fmax 60-90 MHz vs 5.4 MHz). With CoreMark/MHz staying\n  near 2.1-2.2 the fitness should land far above +50% (roughly 10x).\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 50\n  confidence: high\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/muldiv.sv\n    description: \"New sequential M-extension unit (start/busy/done handshake): iterative radix-2 restoring divider and a registered-operand, registered-product single 33x33 signed multiplier.\"\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Drop the combinational MUL*/DIV*/REM* arms; keep the RV32I ops only.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Instantiate muldiv, start it for M-ops, select its result into EX/MEM.alu_result, export ex_busy.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Add ex_busy stall: hold PC and ID/EX, insert bubble into EX/MEM while the M-unit is running.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire ex_busy between ex_stage and hazard_unit.\"\n  - file: test/test_muldiv.py\n    description: \"Cocotb unit test for the sequential M-unit with the RV32M corner vectors.\"\n", "userModified": false}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01PWKb5euCbS1UrJTjPuqrAP", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "config", "reason_type": "mode"}}]}
