{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChLcoiruoPEwa9nAakBCJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015peU9WzwnCPLv5cKe1PfHS","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np='cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261123-002-r1s1.yaml'\ns=open(p).read()\nold=\"\"\"  forward-mux -> 32-bit add/shift/compare -> EX/MEM. Expected Fmax 55-90 MHz\n  (vs 5.44), fitness roughly 120-190 iter/s, i.e. far beyond the +50% the\n  schema field can express.\n\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"  forward-mux -> 32-bit add/shift/compare -> EX/MEM.\n\n  Measured evidence (Gowin P&R, place option 0, throwaway copies of rtl/):\n    - DIV/REM arms stubbed, combinational multiplier kept: Fmax 49.1 MHz,\n      2071 LUT4 (was 12312). Two co-critical paths at ~25.6 ns:\n      (a) regfile -> fwd mux -> multiplier (DSP) -> EX/MEM/dmem address;\n      (b) regfile -> fwd mux -> branch compare -> redirect -> if_stage NOP\n          mux -> hazard_unit load-use compare -> ID/EX enable.\n    - DIV/REM and MUL arms stubbed: 43.8 MHz (same path (b), P&R noise).\n  So this change alone is worth ~45-50 MHz = fitness ~100-110 iter/s (~9x,\n  far beyond the +50% the schema field can express); registering the\n  multiplier removes (a) and item 6 below shortens (b).\n\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new)\nold2=\"\"\"  Invariants untouched:\"\"\"\nnew2=\"\"\"  6. Shorten co-critical path (b): redirect and load_use_hazard are mutually\n     exclusive (both are functions of the SAME ID/EX instruction: redirect\n     needs is_branch/is_jump, load-use needs mem_read), and on redirect\n     flush_id already zeroes ID/EX with priority over stall. So if_stage\n     must stop muxing the IF/ID instruction with NOP on `redirect`: keep the\n     NOP mux for imem_stall only (imem_ready is a flop) and let redirect act\n     only through flush_id and the PC mux. hazard_unit then sees raw\n     instr[19:15]/[24:20] and redirect no longer feeds decode/regfile-read/\n     load-use logic. out.valid may still be gated by redirect.\n  Invariants untouched:\"\"\"\nassert old2 in s; s=s.replace(old2,new2)\nold3=\"\"\"  - file: rtl/core.sv\"\"\"\nnew3=\"\"\"  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Remove `redirect` from the IF/ID instruction NOP mux (NOP only on imem stall); redirect keeps PC priority and kills the wrong-path instruction via flush_id only. Cuts the redirect -> NOP mux -> load-use compare -> ID/EX enable path.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\"\"\"\nassert old3 in s; s=s.replace(old3,new3)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nd=yaml.safe_load(open(p))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('schema OK', d['id'], d['category'], d['expected_impact'], len(d['changes']))\nEOF\ngit status --short | head","description":"Add probe evidence and redirect-path item to the hypothesis, then re-validate schema"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14158,"cache_read_input_tokens":76072,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14158},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1ef5e113-78fa-45f5-9d31-b22c88a410f8","uuid":"a936736b-da18-44b8-9f4e-f9a16fe25499","timestamp":"2026-11-23T22:06:03.884Z","request_id":"req_011ChLcoiiyneBqh5ikFxMkw"}
