{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChLcsgKjep53zJHffkwDu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The hypothesis is written and schema-valid at `cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261123-002-r1s1.yaml`.\n\n**Proposal (structural):** move multiply and divide out of the single-cycle EX path into a sequential M-unit, with the pipeline stalling while it runs.\n\n**Why:** the 199.8 ns worst path is the combinational divider in `alu.sv`. The timed CoreMark region should execute almost no divides and only a few percent multiplies (my estimate, not measured), so the cycle cost should be about 1–3%.\n\n**Timing probe:** I ran Gowin place-and-route (placement option 0) on two throwaway RTL copies; the worktree's `rtl/` is untouched.\n\n| Variant | Fmax | LUT4 |\n|---|---|---|\n| Baseline | 5.44 MHz | 12312 |\n| DIV/REM stubbed out, combinational multiplier kept | 49.1 MHz | 2071 |\n| DIV/REM and MUL stubbed out | 43.8 MHz | 2016 |\n\nRemoving the divider alone is therefore worth roughly 9× Fmax, or a fitness of about 100–110 if cycles per iteration hold. The `fitness_delta_pct` field is set to 50 with high confidence, since the prompt caps it there.\n\nThe probe also showed two co-critical paths at about 25.6 ns once the divider is gone, and the hypothesis addresses both:\n- **Multiplier path:** the three 64-bit combinational multipliers are replaced by one 33×33 signed multiply with registered operands and product.\n- **Branch path:** redirect currently feeds the fetch-stage NOP mux and then the load-use compare. Redirect and load-use can never fire together, so the hypothesis removes redirect from that mux.\n\nThings the implementer must get right, all spelled out in the YAML:\n- **Stale operands:** while an M-op waits in EX its producers retire, so ID/EX operand values must be refreshed with the forwarded values on every held cycle.\n- **Formal window:** under `RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS` the M-unit keeps the same handshake but uses a fixed 2-cycle latency, because a 34-cycle divide cannot retire inside the 20-step check depth.\n- **Test coverage:** every M-extension vector in `test_alu.py` moves unchanged to a new `test_muldiv.py`, so invariant 5b coverage is preserved.\n\nOne side effect I did not check: `make formal-deep` (no ALTOPS, outside the orchestrator loop) may no longer reach a real 34-cycle divide within its depth."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5375,"cache_read_input_tokens":90230,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5375},"output_tokens":798,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1ef5e113-78fa-45f5-9d31-b22c88a410f8","uuid":"db71374a-4b89-4c74-9961-dd708a77a0b9","timestamp":"2026-11-23T22:06:12.998Z","request_id":"req_011ChLcsgCHxPbnVyxYDLsaZ"}
