r\n     state is functionally safe (formal-friendly: no reset-value dependence).\n  5. Training: when a valid conditional branch leaves EX (not held by a dmem\n     stall) update its counter at the carried index and shift the actual\n     outcome into the global history register. Because only ONE instruction\n     is ever speculative (the one in IF/ID while its predecessor is in EX),\n     an instruction that advances into ID/EX is always on the committed path\n     - no history/RAS repair logic is needed.\n  6. Return-address stack (same module, second priority, drop if it\n     endangers formal/timing): 4-entry RAS pushed with pc+4 when a JAL/JALR\n     with rd in {x1,x5} advances into ID/EX, popped when JALR with rs1 in\n     {x1,x5}, rd=x0 advances. Predicted returns carry a 30-bit pred_target in\n     ID/EX; EX redirects only if jalr target != pred_target. Push/pop are\n     gated by the same \"advances into ID/EX\" condition, so the RAS is never\n     corrupted by wrong-path instructions.\n\n  Expected effect: taken branches predicted correctly and all JALs cost 0\n  bubbles instead of 1; mispredicted branches (either direction) cost 1\n  bubble (same as a taken branch today). With ~90% gshare accuracy the\n  redirect rate drops from ~14% of instructions to ~2-3%, removing ~0.11\n  cycles/instruction from a CPI of ~1.45-1.5: about +7-9% CoreMark\n  iterations/cycle at unchanged Fmax.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/branch_predictor.sv\n    description: \"New module: 256x2-bit gshare counter table (async read at fetch, sync update from EX), 8-bit global history register updated with resolved outcomes, and a 4-entry return-address stack with push/pop gated by instruction-advance. All state is prediction-only (verified in EX), so any contents are functionally safe.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add pred_taken, pred_idx[7:0] and pred_target[31:2] (RAS-predicted returns) to if_id_t and id_ex_t.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Pre-decode imem_data for BRANCH/JAL/return, compute pred_target = pc + B/J-imm in the fetch cycle, next PC = redirect ? redirect_target : (pred_taken ? pred_target : pc+4). Gate pred_taken with fetch-valid (no flush/redirect/imem stall) and target alignment; emit pred fields in the IF/ID bundle.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Latch pred_taken / pred_idx / pred_target into the ID/EX register (cleared on flush with the rest of the bundle).\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Redirect only on misprediction: compare actual next-PC decision (branch_taken / jump, minus misalign fault) against pred_taken (and jalr target against pred_target for RAS-predicted returns); redirect_target = actual taken ? target : pc+4. Export branch-resolve training signals (valid conditional branch, taken, pred_idx). pc_next / trap logic unchanged.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Instantiate branch_predictor, wire fetch-side lookup (pc, advance strobe, call/return pre-decode) and EX-side training (gated by !stall_ex_mem so a held branch trains once).\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"No functional change expected (redirect still means 'EX kills the IF/ID instruction'); touch only if the advance strobe for predictor/RAS updates is exported from here (imem_ready && !load_use && !dmem_stall && !redirect).\"\n  - file: test/test_branch_predictor.py\n    description: \"cocotb unit test for branch_predictor: counter saturation/training, gshare index/history update, RAS push/pop ordering and gating, and that predictions never assert for non-advancing fetches.\"\n", "structuredPatch": [], "originalFile": null, "userModified": false}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_019G7Sj18EFUTQvBckdtPAFZ", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "config", "reason_type": "mode"}}]}
