{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChLcqGPmQHHC9QoZNK3sn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The hypothesis is written to `cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261123-003-r1s2.yaml` and validates against the schema.\n\n**Proposal:** fetch-cycle branch prediction — a 256-entry bimodal direction table plus a target computed in the fetch cycle as `pc + imm`, so correctly predicted taken branches and all JALs cost zero bubbles.\n\n**Why this angle:** the core has no IF/ID register, so the fetched instruction is visible in the same cycle as the PC. That means no BTB is needed and the target can never be mispredicted; only the direction is a guess. EX then redirects only on a misprediction.\n\n**Measured on the current RTL** (CoreMark in the Verilator cosim with both bus stalls, first 3.0M cycles):\n- CPI is 1.535, and redirect bubbles are 7.96% of all cycles (12.2% of instructions redirect).\n- Replaying the retirement trace through candidate predictors gave these gains in iterations/cycle:\n\n| Predictor | Branch mispredict | Gain |\n|---|---|---|\n| Static backward-taken | 20.6% | +5.5% |\n| Bimodal 256 (proposed) | 8.45% | +7.1% |\n| Bimodal 1024 | 7.6% | +7.25% |\n| gshare 256 | 8.8–10.7% | +6.8 to +7.1% |\n| gshare 4096 | 6.4% | +7.4% |\n\n- A 4-entry return-address stack would add only +0.35%, so I left it out, along with global history.\n\nAlmost all the gain comes from the zero-bubble target, not predictor sophistication, so the proposal takes the simplest point.\n\n**Expected impact:** +7%, medium confidence. The gain is IPC-only: Fmax is still set by the ~200 ns divider path, which this does not touch. That leaves limited margin over the 4.6% acceptance bar given place-and-route noise of several percent. The trace sample also includes pre-benchmark init code, so the bracketed-region figure may differ slightly.\n\nEvery prediction is verified in EX and the next-PC and trap logic are unchanged, so any predictor state is functionally safe for formal. The YAML spells out the stall/flush cases and the misaligned-target rule for the implementer."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8176,"cache_read_input_tokens":80241,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8176},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2b7c249-c955-42c6-95dd-85292c9d85b9","uuid":"7adb43c7-b9a4-4a15-b7d7-ef9d74355e5c","timestamp":"2026-11-23T22:05:40.433Z","request_id":"req_011ChLcqGD6nU1iZ2655CcVW"}
{"duration_api_ms": 285740, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "session_id": "e2b7c249-c955-42c6-95dd-85292c9d85b9", "total_cost_usd": 2.4958588, "usage": {"input_tokens": 16, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 78447, "cache_read_input_tokens": 486894, "output_tokens": 28580, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 16877}, "server_tool_use": {"web_search_requests": 0, "web_fetch_requests": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 78447, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "inference_geo": "global", "iterations": [], "speed": "standard", "fallback_credit": null}, "modelUsage": {"claude-fable-5-2": {"inputTokens": 16, "outputTokens": 28580, "cacheReadInputTokens": 486894, "cacheCreationInputTokens": 78447, "webSearchRequests": 0, "costUSD": 2.4958588, "contextWindow": 1000000, "maxOutputTokens": 128000, "thinkingTokens": 16877, "cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens": 0, "cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens": 78447, "canonicalModel": "claude-fable-5-2", "provider": "firstParty", "costBasis": "list"}}, "permission_denials": [{"tool_name": "Write", "tool_use_id": "toolu_016YAWyT7W3v657biQna8KZj", "tool_input": {"file_path": "/srv/hwebench/tmp/06925bfd/bp_an.py", "content": "import sys, re\npat = re.compile(r'\"cycle\":(\\d+),\"insn\":(\\d+),\"pc_rdata\":(\\d+),\"pc_wdata\":(\\d+)')\nn = 0\nnbr = nbr_taken = njal = njalr = nret = ncall = 0\nfirst_cycle = None\nlast_cycle = 0\n# predictors\ndef mk(bits): return [1] * (1 << bits)\ncfgs = {}\nfor name, bits, hbits in [(\"bimodal64\", 6, 0), (\"bimodal256\", 8, 0), (\"bimodal1024\", 10, 0),\n                          (\"gshare256h8\", 8, 8), (\"gshare256h6\", 8, 6), (\"gshare1024h10\", 10, 10),\n                          (\"gshare1024h8\", 10, 8), (\"gshare4096h12\", 12, 12), (\"gshare256h4\", 8, 4)]:\n    cfgs[name] = dict(bits=bits, hbits=hbits, tab=mk(bits), ghr=0, miss=0)\nbtfn_miss = 0\nras = []\nras_hit = ras_tot = 0\nfor line in sys.stdin:\n    m = pat.search(line)\n    if not m:\n        continue\n    cyc, insn, pc, npc = map(int, m.groups())\n    if first_cycle is None:\n        first_cycle = cyc\n    last_cycle = cyc\n    n += 1\n    op = insn & 0x7f\n    if op == 0x63:\n        nbr += 1\n        taken = (npc != ((pc + 4) & 0xffffffff))\n        nbr_taken += taken\n        back = (insn >> 31) & 1\n        if bool(back) != bool(taken):\n            btfn_miss += 1\n        for c in cfgs.values():\n            mask = (1 << c[\"bits\"]) - 1\n            idx = ((pc >> 2) ^ (c[\"ghr\"] << (c[\"bits\"] - c[\"hbits\"]) if c[\"hbits\"] else 0)) & mask\n            t = c[\"tab\"][idx]\n            if (t >= 2) != taken:\n                c[\"miss\"] += 1\n            c[\"tab\"][idx] = min(3, t + 1) if taken else max(0, t - 1)\n            if c[\"hbits\"]:\n                c[\"ghr\"] = ((c[\"ghr\"] << 1) | int(taken)) & ((1 << c[\"hbits\"]) - 1)\n    elif op == 0x6f:\n        njal += 1\n        rd = (insn >> 7) & 31\n        if rd in (1, 5):\n            ncall += 1\n            ras.append((pc + 4) & 0xffffffff)\n            ras = ras[-4:]\n    elif op == 0x67:\n        njalr += 1\n        rd = (insn >> 7) & 31\n        rs1 = (insn >> 15) & 31\n        if rs1 in (1, 5) and rd == 0:\n            nret += 1\n            ras_tot += 1\n            if ras and ras[-1] == npc:\n                ras_hit += 1\n            if ras:\n                ras.pop()\n        if rd in (1, 5):\n            ncall += 1\n            ras.append((pc + 4) & 0xffffffff)\n            ras = ras[-4:]\ncycles = last_cycle - first_cycle + 1\nprint(f\"insns={n} cycles={cycles} CPI={cycles/n:.3f}\")\nprint(f\"branches={nbr} ({100*nbr/n:.2f}%) taken={nbr_taken} ({100*nbr_taken/max(1,nbr):.1f}% of br, {100*nbr_taken/n:.2f}% of insns)\")\nprint(f\"jal={njal} ({100*njal/n:.2f}%) jalr={njalr} ({100*njalr/n:.2f}%) ret={nret} ({100*nret/n:.2f}%) ras_hit={ras_hit}/{ras_tot}\")\nredir = nbr_taken + njal + njalr\nprint(f\"baseline redirects={redir} ({100*redir/n:.2f}% of insns, {100*redir/cycles:.2f}% of cycles)\")\nprint(f\"BTFN miss={btfn_miss} ({100*btfn_miss/max(1,nbr):.1f}%)\")\nfor name, c in cfgs.items():\n    miss = c[\"miss\"]\n    # remaining penalties: mispredicted branches + JALR not predicted by RAS\n    rem_ras = miss + (njalr - ras_hit)\n    rem_noras = miss + njalr\n    sv_ras = redir - rem_ras\n    sv_noras = redir - rem_noras\n    print(f\"{name:16s} miss={100*miss/max(1,nbr):5.2f}%  saved cycles: noRAS {100*sv_noras/cycles:.2f}% (speedup {100*(cycles/(cycles-sv_noras)-1):.2f}%)  RAS {100*sv_ras/cycles:.2f}% (speedup {100*(cycles/(cycles-sv_ras)-1):.2f}%)\")\n"}}], "terminal_reason": "completed", "fast_mode_state": "off", "fast_mode_disabled_reason": "sdk_opt_in_required", "subagent_stats": {"spawned": 0, "requested": {"background": 0, "foreground": 0, "unset": 0}, "started_in_background": 0, "max_depth": 0, "spawned_by_subagents": 0, "completed": 0, "failed": 0, "killed": {"parent": 0, "user": 0, "system": 0}, "refused": {"depth_limit": 0, "concurrency_limit": 0, "budget": 0}, "by_type": {}}, "safety_stops": 0, "is_error": false, "num_turns": 10, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "The hypothesis is written to `cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261123-003-r1s2.yaml` and validates against the schema.\n\n**Proposal:** fetch-cycle branch prediction — a 256-entry bimodal direction table plus a target computed in the fetch cycle as `pc + imm`, so correctly predicted taken branches and all JALs cost zero bubbles.\n\n**Why this angle:** the core has no IF/ID register, so the fetched instruction is visible in the same cycle as the PC. That means no BTB is needed and the target can never be mispredicted; only the direction is a guess. EX then redirects only on a misprediction.\n\n**Measured on the current RTL** (CoreMark in the Verilator cosim with both bus stalls, first 3.0M cycles):\n- CPI is 1.535, and redirect bubbles are 7.96% of all cycles (12.2% of instructions redirect).\n- Replaying the retirement trace through candidate predictors gave these gains in iterations/cycle:\n\n| Predictor | Branch mispredict | Gain |\n|---|---|---|\n| Static backward-taken | 20.6% | +5.5% |\n| Bimodal 256 (proposed) | 8.45% | +7.1% |\n| Bimodal 1024 | 7.6% | +7.25% |\n| gshare 256 | 8.8–10.7% | +6.8 to +7.1% |\n| gshare 4096 | 6.4% | +7.4% |\n\n- A 4-entry return-address stack would add only +0.35%, so I left it out, along with global history.\n\nAlmost all the gain comes from the zero-bubble target, not predictor sophistication, so the proposal takes the simplest point.\n\n**Expected impact:** +7%, medium confidence. The gain is IPC-only: Fmax is still set by the ~200 ns divider path, which this does not touch. That leaves limited margin over the 4.6% acceptance bar given place-and-route noise of several percent. The trace sample also includes pre-benchmark init code, so the bracketed-region figure may differ slightly.\n\nEvery prediction is verified in EX and the next-PC and trap logic are unchanged, so any predictor state is functionally safe for formal. The YAML spells out the stall/flush cases and the misaligned-target rule for the implementer.", "ttft_ms": 24910, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 288671, "uuid": "40a46e5b-bf46-44a9-8a6d-0d993bf1ead6", "ttft_stream_ms": 2037, "time_to_request_ms": 228, "first_content_frame_ms": 2037, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0, "model_usage_since_last_result": {"claude-fable-5-2": {"inputTokens": 16, "outputTokens": 28580, "cacheReadInputTokens": 486894, "cacheCreationInputTokens": 78447, "webSearchRequests": 0, "costUSD": 2.4958588, "contextWindow": 1000000, "maxOutputTokens": 128000, "thinkingTokens": 16877, "cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens": 0, "cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens": 78447, "canonicalModel": "claude-fable-5-2", "provider": "firstParty", "costBasis": "list"}}}

